General code layer for C/C++ projects.

It includes platform detection, loggers, allocators, strings, and dynamic array.
Some of the code will work only on Windows and Linux.

Currently supported Platforms are:
    - Windows(MSVC, GCC, Clang) Arch: x86, x64.
    - Linux(GCC, Clang)         Arch: x86, x64.


General Usage: #define GENERAL_IMPLEMENTATION
before #include "general.h"
to include the implementation code.

file.h: 
#define FILE_IMPLEMENTATION
before #include "file.h"

pool.h: 
#define POOL_IMPLEMENTATION
before #include "pool.h"

string_builder.h: 
#define STRING_BUILDER_IMPLEMENTATION
before #include "string_builder.h"

To compile in release, add #define GENERAL_DEBUG 0 before including the file.
